# Installed on top of raye-desktop in the live image. The installer
# removes the live-only ones (casper, calamares) from the new system.
raye-desktop
calamares-settings-raye
casper
language-pack-en
language-pack-fr
language-pack-kde-en
language-pack-kde-fr
language-pack-gnome-fr
hunspell-fr

# Everyday tools, asked for by name (2026-11-03/04). The sizes are what
# each one really costs here, dependencies included, measured against the
# 26.04 archive; the whole list as asked came to 240 MB in 155 packages,
# so what earns its place is kept and the rest is left out.

# Terminal and diagnostics
curl
wget
git
strace
gnupg2
net-tools
htop
btop
mesa-utils

# Managing software: the text one and the piece that add-apt-repository
# lives in. Synaptic is left out: the Store does its work, and it stays
# one install away for those who want it
aptitude
software-properties-common

# The file manager reaches further: Google Drive, printers and shares
# announced on the network, admin folders
kio-gdrive
kde-zeroconf

# A terminal that drops down over the desktop
yakuake

# Sound: the ALSA, JACK and PulseAudio faces of the audio server, and
# cameras for programs that only know V4L2
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-jack
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-v4l2

# Snapshots of the disk, and the filesystem tools behind them
btrfs-assistant
udisks2-btrfs

# Qt programs that are not ours follow the Raye look (to be restyled)
adwaita-qt
adwaita-qt6

# Asked for, and used by other things: async disk I/O, apt over https,
# last-login records, fonts and XML for perl programs
libaio1t64
apt-transport-https
lastlog2
libfont-freetype-perl
libxml-libxml-perl

# The hypervisor can shut this machine down cleanly and freeze its
# filesystem for a consistent snapshot. It costs NOTHING on real
# hardware, and that is measured rather than assumed: the unit is
# `BindsTo=dev-virtio\x2dports-org.qemu.guest_agent.0.device`, so without
# that virtio-serial port -- which a laptop does not have -- systemd
# cannot start it at all. 3.8 MB on a 2.96 GB image, and this beta exists
# to be tried, which for many people means in a VM. Raye already tunes
# for that case (release/tuning/raye-vm-cursor).
qemu-guest-agent
